    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-039: Box Model Completion** — closes ADR-037's deferred height gap and adds four related features. Split into two commits by risk.\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation lands in a follow-up PR (Commit 1: non-risk, Commit 2: box-sizing).\n\n## The gap this closes\n\nADR-037's Implementation section recorded: \"Search icon width 2→20 (correct), height 0 (unchanged). `height` on non-img boxes still unapplied, deferred to ADR-040 box model.\"\n\n**That's this ADR.** `layout_element` applies `width` at line 265, but `height` only inside the `<img>` sizing block from ADR-035. Every non-`<img>` element derives height from content. Applying `height` (or `min-height`) closes the gap.\n\n## Measurement (2026-10-28)\n\n### Usage in Wikipedia CSS\n\n| Property | Total | Dominant values |\n|---|---|---|\n| `box-sizing` | 14 | `border-box` (12), `content-box` (2) |\n| `min-width` | 40 | `10px` (15), `200px` (4), `18.75em` (2), `44px` (2) |\n| `max-width` | 27 | `none` (8), `min(0.85 * 59.25rem, 75vw)` (4), `100%` (3), `320px !important` (1) |\n| `min-height` | 31 | `10px` (15), `32px` (3), `3.125rem` (1 — header) |\n| `max-height` | 6 | `3.3em`, `75vh`, `calc(100vh - 48px)`, `200px`, `2rem` |\n| `overflow` | 18 | `hidden` (13), `auto` (2), `hidden auto` (2), `visible` (1) |\n| `overflow-wrap` | 5 | `break-word` (4), `anywhere` (1) |\n\n### First-viewport impact\n\n| Property | Total | First-viewport |\n|---|---|---|\n| `height` (non-img, currently unapplied) | 7 | **4** |\n| `min-height` | 11 | **9** |\n| `box-sizing` | 9 | **7** |\n| `overflow` | 8 | 5 |\n| `max-width` | 10 | 5 |\n\n## Scope (v1)\n\n### Commit 1 (non-risk, additive)\n\n- **`height` applied to all boxes** — was img-only. Search icon h=0 → h=20.\n- **`min-width` / `max-width` / `min-height` / `max-height` clamps** — after width/height resolution\n- **`overflow: hidden` paint clipping** — Cairo `cairo_rectangle` + `cairo_clip` around children. `LayoutBox::clip_children` set during layout.\n- **vw/vh mitigation** — skip clamp when value contains `vw|vh` AND eval returns 0 (avoids collapse)\n\n### Commit 2 (risk, isolated)\n\n- **`box-sizing: border-box`** — width/height mean border-box. Elements with `box-sizing: border-box` + explicit width shrink by padding+border.\n\n**Why isolated**: this is the highest-risk change in the ADR. Possible visible regressions if the CSS was \"accidentally correct\" at the wrong width. Separate commit for easy revert.\n\n## Two-commit split rationale\n\nThe four features interact (height + max-height clamp, box-sizing + min/max, overflow + height). Committing together keeps interaction tests in one PR. But splitting at the risk boundary lets us:\n\n1. Measure Commit 1's delta cleanly (search icon fix + min-height clamps, no width changes)\n2. Measure Commit 2's delta separately (width shifts, \"did we break anything\")\n3. Revert Commit 2 alone if needed (Commit 1 stays)\n\nSame pattern as ADR-028 shipping the URL fix alongside grid (coupled but isolated in the record).\n\n## What this unblocks (structural value)\n\n`box-sizing` is a **precondition for real CSS layout**:\n- Container queries (future ADR)\n- `aspect-ratio` (future ADR)\n- Flexbox `flex-basis: auto` sizing semantics\n- Any `width: 100%; padding: X` pattern (currently overflows, after ADR-039 fits)\n\nShipping it now unlocks a decade of modern CSS features.\n\n## Deferred\n\n- **`overflow: auto | scroll`** — scrollbar rendering + events, own ADR\n- **`overflow-x` / `overflow-y`** — axis-specific, ship with scroll\n- **`overflow-wrap`** — typography, not box model\n- **`aspect-ratio`** — 0 uses in target CSS\n- **`vw` / `vh` in max-width** — ADR-037 deferred\n- **`overflow: hidden auto`** two-value — treated as `hidden` for both axes for v1\n\n## Test plan\n\nCommit 1 (~10-12 tests in `[layout][box-model][adr-039]` + `[paint][box-model][adr-039]`):\n- height applied, content overflows height, min/max clamps, none/auto no-ops, overflow: hidden clip_children flag, vw-in-max-width skip\n\nCommit 2 (~4-6 tests):\n- box-sizing: border-box subtracts padding, content-box preserved, width 100% + padding fits parent, height equivalent\n\n## Verification after implementation\n\n| Check | Before | Commit 1 | Commit 2 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Search icon | w=20 h=0 | **w=20 h=20** | w=20 h=20 |\n| First-viewport PNG | baseline | search icon visible | box-sizing width shifts |\n| Article body regressions | — | none expected | possible, measured |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Two-commit split accepted** — non-risk (height/min-max/overflow) ships first with clean measurement, box-sizing isolated for revertability\n- [ ] **vw/vh skip-instead-of-collapse accepted** — preserves current render for 4 elements that would otherwise collapse\n- [ ] **`overflow: hidden auto` treated as `hidden`** for both axes — documented limitation\n- [ ] **`overflow: auto | scroll` deferred** — scrollbar + event subsystem, own ADR\n- [ ] **height gap closure tied to ADR-037** — first-viewport visible delta explicitly named\n\nRefs #198\n",
